1
00:00:32,741 --> 00:00:36,202
‎I can picture it… The Spin…

2
00:00:46,796 --> 00:00:48,380
‎It's spinning!

3
00:00:48,381 --> 00:00:49,507
‎Gyro!

4
00:00:53,511 --> 00:00:55,971
‎Gyro, you weren't watching?

5
00:00:55,972 --> 00:00:58,932
‎Why weren't you? It was amazing!

6
00:00:58,933 --> 00:01:01,351
‎The cork spun! I know it did!

7
00:01:01,352 --> 00:01:05,522
‎Why should I keep my eyes on you
‎all the time?

8
00:01:05,523 --> 00:01:08,234
‎So it really spun? Do it again.

9
00:01:10,153 --> 00:01:12,780
‎Huh? That's odd. Where'd the cork go?

10
00:01:12,781 --> 00:01:15,617
‎It couldn't just disappear. Where is it?

11
00:01:16,743 --> 00:01:17,911
‎"Pop"?

12
00:01:19,245 --> 00:01:22,956
‎Where'd that come from?
‎It's a little damp!

13
00:01:22,957 --> 00:01:25,668
‎Don't tell me… the horse's butt…

14
00:01:29,214 --> 00:01:32,342
‎Gyro's bag… What's that?

15
00:01:33,176 --> 00:01:37,095
‎That's a document case
‎with a coat of arms.

16
00:01:37,096 --> 00:01:38,306
‎Did he steal it?

17
00:01:39,015 --> 00:01:44,353
‎In Europe, you need a lord's permission
‎to have a coat of arms.

18
00:01:44,354 --> 00:01:48,817
‎"A boy sentenced to death"?
‎I think I've heard this before.

19
00:01:51,611 --> 00:01:53,278
‎What? "Judicial Officer Zeppeli"?

20
00:01:53,279 --> 00:01:57,325
‎Is that how you were raised?
‎Snooping through other people's things?

21
00:02:18,054 --> 00:02:20,514
‎I wasn't snooping.

22
00:02:20,515 --> 00:02:22,850
‎But who are you?

23
00:02:22,851 --> 00:02:24,726
‎You're not from this country?

24
00:02:24,727 --> 00:02:27,856
‎Just stick to opening your own bags.

25
00:02:31,568 --> 00:02:34,237
‎By the way, someone's over there.

26
00:02:36,030 --> 00:02:40,117
‎What brings someone all the way out here
‎in a desert this big?

27
00:02:40,118 --> 00:02:44,079
‎You said this route was
‎full of weirdos, didn't you?

28
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:47,791
‎I did, but Robinson was a one-off,
‎wasn't he?

29
00:02:47,792 --> 00:02:51,546
‎You never know.
‎You got a weapon on you, Johnny?

30
00:02:52,213 --> 00:02:54,006
‎Then have it ready.

31
00:02:54,007 --> 00:02:57,801
‎I've got a gun. But I've never fired one.

32
00:02:57,802 --> 00:03:00,305
‎If he gets any closer,
‎we'll drive him off!

33
00:04:32,689 --> 00:04:35,732
‎First to the watering hole

34
00:04:35,733 --> 00:04:38,193
‎were Pocoloco, Sand Man, and Diego Brando.

35
00:04:38,194 --> 00:04:41,823
‎It's a predictable outcome
‎for the first day of the second stage.

36
00:04:43,825 --> 00:04:46,785
‎Didn't some competitors
‎take another route?

37
00:04:46,786 --> 00:04:49,788
‎That would be Gyro Zeppeli
‎and Johnny Joestar.

38
00:04:49,789 --> 00:04:53,709
‎They're camped deep in the desert,
‎about 60 miles from the start.

39
00:04:53,710 --> 00:04:57,587
‎Robinson, who took the same route,
‎retired after sustaining an injury.

40
00:04:57,588 --> 00:05:00,007
‎So they're the only two on that route?

41
00:05:00,008 --> 00:05:02,802
‎No, sir. There are several others as well.

42
00:05:03,803 --> 00:05:06,179
‎Is he really going to ride all night?

43
00:05:06,180 --> 00:05:09,142
‎Impossible.
‎He'd only end up hurting his horse.

44
00:05:09,684 --> 00:05:12,477
‎The observation balloons
‎seem to have landed already.

45
00:05:12,478 --> 00:05:16,815
‎Looks like this route's open
‎to interference now.

46
00:05:16,816 --> 00:05:18,358
‎Do you think so?

47
00:05:18,359 --> 00:05:20,987
‎All right! Stop right there!

48
00:05:21,571 --> 00:05:23,530
‎Don't take another step!

49
00:05:23,531 --> 00:05:25,825
‎Stop, or I'll shoot!

50
00:05:27,869 --> 00:05:30,162
‎You! I'm talking to you!

51
00:05:30,163 --> 00:05:32,622
‎I said stop right there!

52
00:05:32,623 --> 00:05:34,375
‎You wanna get shot?

53
00:05:35,543 --> 00:05:37,586
‎Please don't shoot!

54
00:05:37,587 --> 00:05:39,338
‎I'm Andrew Boomboom!

55
00:05:39,339 --> 00:05:41,089
‎I'm no threat!

56
00:05:41,090 --> 00:05:43,800
‎I saw your campfire and came over!

57
00:05:43,801 --> 00:05:46,094
‎Whether you're a threat or not,

58
00:05:46,095 --> 00:05:48,388
‎I'll decide after you're gone.

59
00:05:48,389 --> 00:05:51,433
‎I'm in trouble. Big trouble!

60
00:05:51,434 --> 00:05:54,103
‎I got bitten!

61
00:05:54,729 --> 00:05:57,814
‎I squatted to take a crap,
‎then went to wipe my ass…

62
00:05:57,815 --> 00:06:00,358
‎It was hiding behind my crap!

63
00:06:00,359 --> 00:06:01,610
‎Damn it all!

64
00:06:01,611 --> 00:06:04,196
‎Johnny, what did he say bit him?

65
00:06:04,197 --> 00:06:05,864
‎He hasn't said yet.

66
00:06:05,865 --> 00:06:09,034
‎Hey! Why'd you get off your horse,
‎you bastard?

67
00:06:09,035 --> 00:06:10,702
‎I said, stay back!

68
00:06:10,703 --> 00:06:14,289
‎It was a venomous lizard.
‎Yellow with black stripes!

69
00:06:14,290 --> 00:06:17,000
‎Please. Let me use your fire!

70
00:06:17,001 --> 00:06:20,545
‎I need that fire to burn the wound clean!

71
00:06:20,546 --> 00:06:22,339
‎The wound could be fake.

72
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:25,967
‎If it was yellow with black stripes,
‎that's a spotted salamander.

73
00:06:25,968 --> 00:06:27,762
‎If the venom spreads, you're dead.

74
00:06:29,305 --> 00:06:32,516
‎Tough luck. Wait for the rescue team.

75
00:06:32,517 --> 00:06:36,394
‎Are you kidding?
‎They're not coming out here at night!

76
00:06:36,395 --> 00:06:39,148
‎I'll be dead by morning.

77
00:06:39,899 --> 00:06:42,317
‎I need to cut the venom out with a knife,

78
00:06:42,318 --> 00:06:44,319
‎then burn the wound clean!

79
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:47,280
‎Give me some fire!

80
00:06:47,281 --> 00:06:48,949
‎You'll let him die?

81
00:06:48,950 --> 00:06:52,410
‎Who knows? I don't trust him.

82
00:06:52,411 --> 00:06:53,871
‎He's a weird one.

83
00:06:54,872 --> 00:06:56,957
‎You're not getting any closer!

84
00:06:56,958 --> 00:06:59,543
‎But I'll give you a burning log.

85
00:06:59,544 --> 00:07:02,088
‎Start your own fire
‎and cauterize your wound.

86
00:07:03,131 --> 00:07:06,967
‎Thank you, thank you, thank you!

87
00:07:06,968 --> 00:07:09,052
‎Thank you, thank you!

88
00:07:09,053 --> 00:07:11,513
‎Thank you, thank you, thank you!

89
00:07:11,514 --> 00:07:12,932
‎Thank you!

90
00:07:28,948 --> 00:07:30,449
‎Hey! What are you doing?

91
00:07:30,450 --> 00:07:33,618
‎It's just an anesthetic.

92
00:07:33,619 --> 00:07:35,287
‎I'm cutting out

93
00:07:35,288 --> 00:07:38,415
‎the poisoned flesh.

94
00:07:38,416 --> 00:07:40,793
‎I need a painkiller, right?

95
00:07:42,128 --> 00:07:45,547
‎It's a crazy trick only I came up with.

96
00:07:45,548 --> 00:07:48,425
‎I always have girls choke me.

97
00:07:48,426 --> 00:07:50,261
‎Don't steal my idea.

98
00:07:51,762 --> 00:07:55,557
‎Right to the edge of blacking out!

99
00:07:55,558 --> 00:07:57,267
‎What is he talking about?

100
00:07:57,268 --> 00:07:59,687
‎No idea! What's with him?

101
00:08:17,205 --> 00:08:20,540
‎Oh, no! He actually cut the wound open!

102
00:08:20,541 --> 00:08:22,751
‎He really got bitten by the lizard!

103
00:08:22,752 --> 00:08:26,379
‎Shit! Of all things to see before bed…

104
00:08:26,380 --> 00:08:28,423
‎All right, here's your fire!

105
00:08:28,424 --> 00:08:31,052
‎Now get the hell out of here!

106
00:08:32,929 --> 00:08:34,305
‎He's not moving.

107
00:08:35,056 --> 00:08:38,684
‎Maybe he really went too far… Damn it.

108
00:08:39,727 --> 00:08:43,230
‎Hey! Wake up!
‎Sorry I was so cold to you, but…

109
00:08:43,231 --> 00:08:46,483
‎You can't just lie there all night.

110
00:08:46,484 --> 00:08:48,903
‎Get up and leave now.

111
00:08:51,197 --> 00:08:54,616
‎Hey. Don't tell me you're really dead.

112
00:08:54,617 --> 00:08:57,994
‎Gyro, his name
‎is on the list of competitors.

113
00:08:57,995 --> 00:09:01,499
‎Andrew Boomboom.
‎He finished tenth in the first stage.

114
00:09:11,551 --> 00:09:14,761
‎Wait. Ninth was Benny Boomboom.

115
00:09:14,762 --> 00:09:17,973
‎Eleventh was Laurence Boomboom…
‎Same last name.

116
00:09:17,974 --> 00:09:20,393
‎There are three of them… A family?

117
00:09:30,361 --> 00:09:33,363
‎Do you think Andrew's dead?

118
00:09:33,364 --> 00:09:36,116
‎Dad! Is Andrew really dead?

119
00:09:36,117 --> 00:09:39,452
‎Shut up, you moron! Men don't cry!

120
00:09:39,453 --> 00:09:41,204
‎Never mind that. Gyro Zeppeli…

121
00:09:41,205 --> 00:09:45,167
‎He touched Andrew's bloodstained knife!

122
00:09:51,299 --> 00:09:53,174
‎Two riders are coming this way!

123
00:09:53,175 --> 00:09:55,051
‎They're a team of three.

124
00:09:55,052 --> 00:09:57,263
‎If they keep coming at us…

125
00:09:58,848 --> 00:10:01,808
‎Johnny! Shoot the one on the right!

126
00:10:01,809 --> 00:10:03,102
‎I'll take the left!

127
00:10:05,396 --> 00:10:08,189
‎What? What's this? My foot…

128
00:10:08,190 --> 00:10:10,066
‎Gyro! What the hell is…

129
00:10:10,067 --> 00:10:14,487
‎No idea! The skin on my left leg
‎is as hard as steel.

130
00:10:14,488 --> 00:10:17,365
‎It feels like
‎there's something solid inside it!

131
00:10:17,366 --> 00:10:20,243
‎Was it Andrew Boomboom?

132
00:10:20,244 --> 00:10:23,580
‎Or was it those two coming this way?

133
00:10:23,581 --> 00:10:26,124
‎It's got to be one or the other!

134
00:10:26,125 --> 00:10:28,418
‎But I don't know what they did to me!

135
00:10:28,419 --> 00:10:30,337
‎Something's wrong with my body!

136
00:10:30,338 --> 00:10:34,091
‎Did they poison me
‎or infect me with some disease?

137
00:10:35,426 --> 00:10:37,510
‎Here they come! Just take the right!

138
00:10:37,511 --> 00:10:39,722
‎Don't let them get any closer!

139
00:10:43,434 --> 00:10:44,435
‎What?

140
00:10:45,936 --> 00:10:46,979
‎Gyro!

141
00:10:52,193 --> 00:10:53,735
‎Johnny! What are you doing?

142
00:10:53,736 --> 00:10:56,529
‎My gun suddenly fell apart!

143
00:10:56,530 --> 00:10:58,949
‎It's not even old!

144
00:11:00,785 --> 00:11:02,994
‎Something's pulling my gun.

145
00:11:02,995 --> 00:11:04,872
‎Toward you!

146
00:11:10,711 --> 00:11:12,505
‎What the…

147
00:11:17,426 --> 00:11:21,180
‎Gyro! The knife's moving toward you too!

148
00:11:33,234 --> 00:11:35,902
‎Andrew's not moving.

149
00:11:35,903 --> 00:11:38,655
‎I hope he got the lizard poison out.

150
00:11:38,656 --> 00:11:42,534
‎Hey, Laurence.
‎Why're you still glued to my ass?

151
00:11:42,535 --> 00:11:45,870
‎I told you to circle around behind them.

152
00:11:45,871 --> 00:11:47,914
‎Our plan's simple.

153
00:11:47,915 --> 00:11:51,084
‎Trap them between us, and that's it!

154
00:11:51,085 --> 00:11:54,587
‎You're so damn slow.
‎Just like your mother.

155
00:11:54,588 --> 00:11:57,090
‎Isn't our mom a stork?

156
00:11:57,091 --> 00:11:59,801
‎Andrew said so. Do I look like a stork?

157
00:11:59,802 --> 00:12:02,762
‎Enough! Get around to the other side!

158
00:12:02,763 --> 00:12:04,639
‎Okay.

159
00:12:04,640 --> 00:12:07,142
‎Gyro, that knife is made of iron.

160
00:12:07,143 --> 00:12:09,936
‎The gun parts going into you are iron too.

161
00:12:09,937 --> 00:12:12,565
‎Isn't the iron being pulled toward you?

162
00:12:13,774 --> 00:12:15,733
‎Your blood has iron in it too.

163
00:12:15,734 --> 00:12:19,113
‎Maybe they're controlling iron somehow!

164
00:12:55,065 --> 00:12:58,152
‎The Steel Ball was shaved away in midair!

165
00:13:01,405 --> 00:13:05,575
‎Dad's in first. Andrew's in second.
‎And I'm in third.

166
00:13:05,576 --> 00:13:09,412
‎That's a lot of prize money!
‎Together, that's a fortune!

167
00:13:09,413 --> 00:13:11,873
‎Well, how much is that altogether?

168
00:13:11,874 --> 00:13:14,751
‎51.5 million dollars, you moron!

169
00:13:14,752 --> 00:13:17,462
‎Gyro! The Steel Balls
‎are made of iron too!

170
00:13:17,463 --> 00:13:19,756
‎But what could shave iron down like that?

171
00:13:19,757 --> 00:13:21,592
‎Who the hell are these guys?

172
00:13:22,218 --> 00:13:25,803
‎We're surrounded, Gyro!
‎They're circling us!

173
00:13:25,804 --> 00:13:27,847
‎These men are different.

174
00:13:27,848 --> 00:13:31,601
‎They're in a completely different league
‎from Robinson.

175
00:13:31,602 --> 00:13:36,064
‎They entered this race
‎with something beyond human ability!

176
00:13:36,065 --> 00:13:38,900
‎What do you mean?
‎What's "beyond human ability"?

177
00:13:38,901 --> 00:13:42,654
‎I don't know.
‎That's just the feeling I get.

178
00:13:42,655 --> 00:13:44,532
‎Nothing else makes sense.

179
00:13:48,536 --> 00:13:52,414
‎Gyro! That crazy bastard's awake!

180
00:14:02,049 --> 00:14:03,509
‎Gh… Ghgh…

181
00:14:04,301 --> 00:14:07,428
‎Andrew! You're awake!

182
00:14:07,429 --> 00:14:08,763
‎Is the venom gone?

183
00:14:08,764 --> 00:14:10,181
‎Shut up!

184
00:14:10,182 --> 00:14:12,308
‎Johnny! Did you see that? What was that?

185
00:14:12,309 --> 00:14:13,352
‎Huh? What?

186
00:14:14,436 --> 00:14:15,895
‎It's gone.

187
00:14:15,896 --> 00:14:18,064
‎Never mind that! Gyro, your leg!

188
00:14:18,065 --> 00:14:22,527
‎I know. It's gotten worse
‎since they surrounded us.

189
00:14:22,528 --> 00:14:24,487
‎This is a coordinated attack.

190
00:14:24,488 --> 00:14:27,407
‎The closer they get,

191
00:14:27,408 --> 00:14:30,578
‎the more strongly
‎the iron in me affects my body.

192
00:14:31,203 --> 00:14:33,371
‎If they get any closer,

193
00:14:33,372 --> 00:14:35,833
‎it may pierce right through me.

194
00:14:36,667 --> 00:14:39,252
‎Johnny, are you okay?

195
00:14:39,253 --> 00:14:41,087
‎Yeah, I'm fine.

196
00:14:41,088 --> 00:14:43,299
‎Maybe touching it did it.

197
00:14:43,966 --> 00:14:47,343
‎You touched his bloodstained knife.

198
00:14:47,344 --> 00:14:49,178
‎Hey, Laurence.

199
00:14:49,179 --> 00:14:51,473
‎-Yeah?
‎-Can you do this?

200
00:14:53,350 --> 00:14:56,853
‎Squashed nostrils!

201
00:14:56,854 --> 00:14:58,730
‎Whoa! That's awesome!

202
00:14:58,731 --> 00:15:01,566
‎You're amazing, Andrew! How'd you do that?

203
00:15:01,567 --> 00:15:03,818
‎No way, you moron! I'm not telling.

204
00:15:03,819 --> 00:15:06,738
‎You couldn't do it in a million years.

205
00:15:06,739 --> 00:15:10,241
‎Come on! Tell me! Tell me!

206
00:15:10,242 --> 00:15:13,579
‎Please, Andrew! What's the harm?

207
00:15:14,413 --> 00:15:16,497
‎My ears fit into my ear holes!

208
00:15:16,498 --> 00:15:17,665
‎They're all squashed!

209
00:15:17,666 --> 00:15:19,375
‎Whoa! Amazing!

210
00:15:19,376 --> 00:15:20,710
‎Hey! You two!

211
00:15:20,711 --> 00:15:23,671
‎Who's going in to finish them off?

212
00:15:23,672 --> 00:15:24,840
‎Do I have to?

213
00:15:25,382 --> 00:15:28,968
‎The guy on horseback…
‎He might have more guns.

214
00:15:28,969 --> 00:15:32,847
‎He doesn't. And even if he did, so what?

215
00:15:32,848 --> 00:15:34,557
‎I guess you're right.

216
00:15:34,558 --> 00:15:36,517
‎Then I'll go, Dad.

217
00:15:36,518 --> 00:15:39,103
‎They didn't give me the fire right away.

218
00:15:39,104 --> 00:15:42,815
‎I was this close to the venom spreading
‎through my whole body.

219
00:15:42,816 --> 00:15:45,319
‎I'm gonna make them pay!

220
00:15:50,824 --> 00:15:55,036
‎Hey, look. He pulled out
‎another steel ball.

221
00:15:55,037 --> 00:15:56,204
‎Gyro…

222
00:15:56,205 --> 00:15:58,290
‎Johnny, load the gear onto the horses.

223
00:16:01,669 --> 00:16:05,713
‎Here we go again.
‎Does he think it'll reach Andrew?

224
00:16:05,714 --> 00:16:08,174
‎He'll probably throw it again.

225
00:16:08,175 --> 00:16:13,763
‎He has no idea
‎Andrew's the best of the Boomboom family.

226
00:16:13,764 --> 00:16:17,309
‎Here I come! I'll rip your guts out!

227
00:16:18,727 --> 00:16:20,062
‎Not a chance, idiot!

228
00:16:23,649 --> 00:16:25,483
‎So he changed its trajectory?

229
00:16:25,484 --> 00:16:27,568
‎Makes no difference.

230
00:16:27,569 --> 00:16:30,656
‎It'll never get anywhere near me!

231
00:16:36,829 --> 00:16:39,998
‎It seems their ability only affects iron.

232
00:16:39,999 --> 00:16:41,917
‎Stone isn't affected.

233
00:16:42,918 --> 00:16:46,254
‎It hurts! Dad!

234
00:16:46,255 --> 00:16:49,716
‎Andrew's got a hole in his gut!

235
00:16:49,717 --> 00:16:51,551
‎That's awful!

236
00:16:51,552 --> 00:16:54,387
‎It's bigger than his belly button!

237
00:16:54,388 --> 00:16:56,389
‎We have to get out of here.

238
00:16:56,390 --> 00:16:57,516
‎-Let's go, Johnny!
‎-Right!

239
00:17:02,563 --> 00:17:04,605
‎They're running away!

240
00:17:04,606 --> 00:17:06,650
‎You're not getting away, you pigs!

241
00:17:08,152 --> 00:17:12,655
‎Dad, they're too far away.
‎And bullets are made of lead.

242
00:17:12,656 --> 00:17:16,743
‎I know that! Since when
‎did you become Mr. Know-It-All?

243
00:17:16,744 --> 00:17:20,455
‎Don't act like you know everything
‎with that tiny brain of yours!

244
00:17:20,456 --> 00:17:22,832
‎Hey, Andrew!
‎Scoot over to the right a bit.

245
00:17:22,833 --> 00:17:23,876
‎Right!

246
00:17:37,598 --> 00:17:40,475
‎Damn bastards… That'll do.

247
00:17:40,476 --> 00:17:41,893
‎Let me see your wounds.

248
00:17:41,894 --> 00:17:44,771
‎-Dad, I'm gonna die.
‎-That's a pretty small hole.

249
00:17:44,772 --> 00:17:49,275
‎When I was younger, I fell off a cliff
‎and blew my jaw clean off.

250
00:17:49,276 --> 00:17:52,028
‎-Then I walked three miles home.
‎-He'll pay!

251
00:17:52,029 --> 00:17:54,280
‎I'll get even!

252
00:17:54,281 --> 00:17:58,618
‎Yeah! We'll kill those two
‎and take first place in the second stage!

253
00:17:58,619 --> 00:18:02,539
‎And we've got an even bigger bonus
‎waiting for us!

254
00:18:04,875 --> 00:18:06,918
‎But how are we gonna catch them?

255
00:18:06,919 --> 00:18:11,172
‎Aren't we attacking them
‎because we can't just catch them?

256
00:18:11,173 --> 00:18:15,218
‎There he goes…
‎Our little genius has an opinion.

257
00:18:15,219 --> 00:18:16,636
‎Stupid little brain.

258
00:18:16,637 --> 00:18:19,097
‎Who ever said we'd be chasing them?

259
00:18:19,098 --> 00:18:21,140
‎We'll let the one behind us

260
00:18:21,141 --> 00:18:24,435
‎chase Gyro Zeppeli and Johnny Joestar
‎and finish them off!

261
00:18:24,436 --> 00:18:25,728
‎What? Behind us?

262
00:18:25,729 --> 00:18:28,106
‎Who's the one behind us?

263
00:18:28,107 --> 00:18:30,942
‎The one who's been tracking me!

264
00:18:30,943 --> 00:18:35,571
‎Someone's been following
‎only my horseshoe prints this whole time.

265
00:18:35,572 --> 00:18:38,909
‎I've known it all along!

266
00:18:39,451 --> 00:18:42,913
‎You mean these tracks, Dad?
‎Someone was following them?

267
00:18:43,497 --> 00:18:47,208
‎Probably a deputy…
‎Most likely Mountain Tim!

268
00:18:47,209 --> 00:18:48,626
‎Mountain Tim?

269
00:18:48,627 --> 00:18:51,504
‎Wow! Everyone's favorite cowboy!

270
00:18:51,505 --> 00:18:54,340
‎He's close to the sheriff, apparently.

271
00:18:54,341 --> 00:18:57,760
‎It's the cowboy, Andrew! He's after us!

272
00:18:57,761 --> 00:18:59,929
‎That's the problem, you moron!

273
00:18:59,930 --> 00:19:02,557
‎We're gonna turn that to our advantage.

274
00:19:02,558 --> 00:19:05,435
‎With our ability to control iron!

275
00:19:06,311 --> 00:19:10,774
‎Do you remember when we gained this power?

276
00:19:11,692 --> 00:19:12,775
‎Yeah, Dad.

277
00:19:12,776 --> 00:19:16,237
‎That place the Native Americans shunned…

278
00:19:16,238 --> 00:19:20,867
‎We got this power while searching for
‎a mine at the Devil's Palm!

279
00:19:20,868 --> 00:19:25,454
‎They said it'd bring misfortune,
‎but it brought us fortune!

280
00:19:25,455 --> 00:19:28,207
‎We'll eliminate anyone
‎who stands in our way!

281
00:19:28,208 --> 00:19:33,130
‎This Boomboom family
‎will stay in first place!

282
00:19:41,722 --> 00:19:46,684
‎I was just about to resume the pursuit
‎in the morning.

283
00:19:46,685 --> 00:19:49,812
‎Under the laws of the U.S.
‎and the Arizona Territory,

284
00:19:49,813 --> 00:19:52,690
‎I have been appointed deputy sheriff.

285
00:19:52,691 --> 00:19:56,777
‎You're under arrest on suspicion
‎of murdering three competitors.

286
00:19:56,778 --> 00:19:58,822
‎Show me your hands and come out slowly.

287
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:03,076
‎I'll use force if I have to.

288
00:20:05,913 --> 00:20:08,290
‎Turn around! Keep your hands up.

289
00:20:12,544 --> 00:20:15,672
‎You're the one who finished fifth?

290
00:20:25,265 --> 00:20:27,308
‎What are you trying to do?

291
00:20:27,309 --> 00:20:30,771
‎I'd like to end this pursuit here
‎and focus on the race.

292
00:20:31,813 --> 00:20:32,940
‎Not so fast.

293
00:20:41,073 --> 00:20:44,660
‎Are you coming out, or do I drag you out?

294
00:20:47,329 --> 00:20:50,999
‎This rope… You're mocking me…

295
00:20:53,126 --> 00:20:54,586
‎What? What the…

296
00:21:13,105 --> 00:21:16,566
‎This is…! No way, Mountain Tim!

297
00:21:17,150 --> 00:21:20,779
‎You're another cursed man
‎who's been to that place?

298
00:21:22,739 --> 00:21:25,574
‎So this is the one who's been tracking us!

299
00:21:25,575 --> 00:21:28,077
‎But either way, we're still the winners!

300
00:21:28,078 --> 00:21:30,997
‎He touched that horseshoe,

301
00:21:30,998 --> 00:21:34,333
‎and now he's touched me too!

302
00:21:34,334 --> 00:21:36,670
‎He's finished!

303
00:21:42,259 --> 00:21:45,554
‎That's a surprise.
‎His name must be Johnny Joestar.

304
00:21:46,305 --> 00:21:48,597
‎So it was him.

305
00:21:48,598 --> 00:21:52,351
‎The setup's complete.
‎Now we just sit back and watch!

306
00:21:52,352 --> 00:21:56,897
‎Once that cowboy catches up to
‎Johnny Joestar and Gyro Zeppeli,

307
00:21:56,898 --> 00:21:59,859
‎the three of them
‎will be pulled together by magnetism.

308
00:21:59,860 --> 00:22:04,156
‎Then they'll tear themselves apart
‎and spill their guts!

309
00:23:30,951 --> 00:23:35,956
‎Subtitle translation by:
‎Ryoko Quirke
